<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Álvaro I of Kongo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1587">1587</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Álvaro I was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-kongo">Kongo</a> from 1568 to 1587. Early in his reign invaders known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaga">Jaga</a> overran the kingdom and drove him from his capital, São <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador">Salvador</a>, to an island in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congo-river">Congo River</a>, and he was restored in the early 1570s with the help of Portuguese troops sent from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sao-tome">São Tomé</a>. He promoted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a>, and his reign saw the Portuguese establish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luanda">Luanda</a> to the south in 1576.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alvaro-i-of-kongo.jpg" alt="Álvaro I of Kongo" width="320" height="440" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Congoking.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The kingdom also fought neighbouring states and rival claimants to the throne, and in 1568 invaders known as the Jaga briefly drove King <b>Álvaro I</b> from his capital until Portuguese troops helped restore him.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kongo-empire">Kongo Empire · Military</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mbanza-kongo">M'banza-Kongo</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/angola">Angola</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mbanza-kongo">M'banza-Kongo</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/angola">Angola</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=-6.27,14.25&amp;year=1577" aria-label="M'banza-Kongo on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4945 2398 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Álvaro I of Kongo"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5395 2668h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5395 2668h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=-6.27,14.25&amp;year=1577">What was here in 1577? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
